1
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:14,700
[Connecting to You]

2
00:01:16,210 --> 00:01:18,260
["Night School Boys" is out.]
[Wanna watch it together?]

3
00:01:18,289 --> 00:01:20,120
[Are you cooking dinner?]

4
00:01:22,190 --> 00:01:24,130
Why are you back, Senior?

5
00:01:24,410 --> 00:01:26,530
Weren't you going to buy lunch?

6
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:31,210
Did you have a fight with Jiakai?

7
00:01:34,910 --> 00:01:36,250
I was too lazy to go out,

8
00:01:36,250 --> 00:01:38,370
so I asked Lai to buy it for me.

9
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:42,460
So, was the fight about cleaning
or washing dishes?

10
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,690
How could we fight
over such trivial things?

11
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:51,700
No.

12
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:54,350
We don't live together,
so how could we fight over those things?

13
00:01:54,350 --> 00:01:56,000
Don't be so nervous.

14
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:58,220
Don't worry. I won't tell anyone.

15
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,430
But I noticed you guys
haven't been talking much lately.

16
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:03,890
What's it about?

17
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:05,690
[Keke]

18
00:02:05,410 --> 00:02:06,280
Keke.

19
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:07,960
Why does she have your number?

20
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:09,820
What does she want from you?

21
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:12,000
We just agreed to watch a movie together.

22
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,030
Which one and where?

23
00:02:17,010 --> 00:02:19,570
Are you interrogating me
like a suspect now?

24
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:22,160
You're the one not to tell the truth.

25
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:24,940
I don't want to talk about it.

26
00:02:25,290 --> 00:02:26,750
It's my private business.

27
00:02:35,410 --> 00:02:36,480
Just...

28
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:39,000
nothing.

29
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:54,790
[The 8th Thread]

30
00:02:54,810 --> 00:03:04,260
[Reaction Formation]
[His Prickly Attitude Isn't Intentional]

31
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:57,250
It's been so long.

32
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:59,450
Is Professor Zeng really coming today?

33
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:02,720
I confirmed with the department office.

34
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:03,870
Professor Zeng will be in the lab

35
00:03:03,870 --> 00:03:06,500
between 3:00 and 6:00 p.m.

36
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:14,260
[The Department Student Association
Welcomes You]

37
00:03:07,210 --> 00:03:09,300
I don't know why he isn't here yet.

38
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:12,320
But we've been waiting for over an hour.

39
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:17,210
Maybe we should just forget it.

40
00:03:17,690 --> 00:03:19,920
I think I'll make an appointment
with Professor Zeng next time

41
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:20,980
and come back then.

42
00:03:22,079 --> 00:03:22,620
Okay.

43
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Do you have classes this afternoon?

44
00:03:27,570 --> 00:03:28,890
No classes this afternoon.

45
00:03:28,890 --> 00:03:30,960
Great. I'll take you somewhere.

46
00:03:31,350 --> 00:03:32,220
Where?

47
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:34,500
Just follow me, and you'll see. Hurry up.

48
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,000
Right here?

49
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:55,090
Welcome to the Old House Bookstore.

50
00:03:56,150 --> 00:03:58,360
The layout here is so unique.

51
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:01,430
It looks a bit like
my grandparents' old house.

52
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:04,390
That's right.
This used to be my grandpa's house.

53
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:06,840
After my grandpa passed away
a few years ago,

54
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:09,590
my dad considered selling it.

55
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:10,490
But

56
00:04:10,510 --> 00:04:12,690
my sister and I couldn't bear
to part with it,

57
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:14,400
so we begged him

58
00:04:14,430 --> 00:04:17,060
to let us turn it into a bookstore.

59
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:19,079
My sister is in charge of
the behind-the-scenes planning,

60
00:04:19,079 --> 00:04:21,680
and I'm in charge of
the frontline operations.

61
00:04:22,510 --> 00:04:24,670
How long did it take you

62
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:27,110
to transform it into what it is now?

63
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,180
A long time.

64
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:32,870
Because we insisted on
drawing the blueprints ourselves,

65
00:04:32,870 --> 00:04:35,350
the design alone took a lot of time.

66
00:04:35,370 --> 00:04:37,120
After the design was finished,

67
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:39,860
we had to find contractors
to do the renovation

68
00:04:39,890 --> 00:04:43,010
and make all the bookshelves,
tables, and chairs.

69
00:04:43,350 --> 00:04:44,760
Of course, we also kept a lot of

70
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:46,510
things left by my grandpa.

71
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,160
Why was I peeking? That's her privacy.

72
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:10,360
What are you doing?

73
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:15,930
My hands were itchy.
Just a pat, and it'll be fine.

74
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:27,620
You're back.

75
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:35,320
What took you so long?

76
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:37,140
Weren't you going to cook ramen?

77
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:40,080
Because you didn't reply to my messages,

78
00:05:40,110 --> 00:05:41,850
I ate before coming back.

79
00:05:42,150 --> 00:05:43,530
Are you full?

80
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:45,770
Of course, I'm full.

81
00:05:45,770 --> 00:05:47,100
How could I wait for you?

82
00:05:49,790 --> 00:05:52,540
Then I'll cook ramen next time.

83
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:58,430
Why is there a bagpack here?

84
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:04,930
I don't know.

85
00:06:13,980 --> 00:06:16,380
How long have you
been using that backpack?

86
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:18,840
Three years.

87
00:06:19,730 --> 00:06:21,390
It can still last a bit longer.

88
00:06:22,930 --> 00:06:24,560
Is it for me?

89
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:30,780
Good that it's not.

90
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:34,140
Because I also bought one today.

91
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:36,170
You bought a new one too?

92
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:37,000
Yeah.

93
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:38,350
Did you buy it yourself?

94
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:41,159
With Chaonan?

95
00:06:42,190 --> 00:06:43,020
Keke?

96
00:06:51,430 --> 00:06:53,830
Anyway, it's not for you.
Don't ask so much.

97
00:06:56,010 --> 00:06:56,840
Good night.

98
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:12,360
Really? No way.

99
00:07:13,690 --> 00:07:14,810
Wait, I see my friend.

100
00:07:14,810 --> 00:07:16,740
You go first. I'll come over later.

101
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:21,290
Why are you playing
a two-player game alone?

102
00:07:21,290 --> 00:07:22,670
So lonely.

103
00:07:22,690 --> 00:07:23,670
Mind your own business.

104
00:07:23,670 --> 00:07:24,950
What are you doing here?

105
00:07:24,950 --> 00:07:26,200
Just playing.

106
00:07:28,070 --> 00:07:29,520
Oh my god.

107
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:30,870
Except for my grandma,

108
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:32,120
I've never seen anyone play Taiko Master

109
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,740
so badly.

110
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:37,980
Let me show you who the real

111
00:07:38,010 --> 00:07:39,480
Taiko Master is.

112
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:00,290
Can I ask you something?

113
00:08:00,350 --> 00:08:01,520
Sure.

114
00:08:01,610 --> 00:08:03,510
As a Taiko Master, I'll never
hide anything.

115
00:08:03,510 --> 00:08:04,760
Come on, go ahead.

116
00:08:05,710 --> 00:08:07,240
I just wanted to ask you that

117
00:08:07,970 --> 00:08:11,500
Jiakai said the threads tied to you
were once severely tangled.

118
00:08:12,190 --> 00:08:14,570
That means a bunch of threads
were tied to you, right?

119
00:08:14,570 --> 00:08:16,830
I thought you didn't believe it at first.

120
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:17,910
Right.

121
00:08:17,930 --> 00:08:21,050
According to Jiakai,
there were indeed many threads.

122
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:23,430
Did Jiakai ever say

123
00:08:23,450 --> 00:08:25,510
how many threads were tied to him?

124
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:27,010
Why do you ask?

125
00:08:27,930 --> 00:08:29,170
I was just thinking,

126
00:08:30,190 --> 00:08:32,120
since every time he helps someone,

127
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:35,260
a thread is created between them,

128
00:08:36,039 --> 00:08:38,770
he should also be someone
with a bunch of threads.

129
00:08:38,890 --> 00:08:41,090
If that were the case, it would be great.

130
00:08:41,770 --> 00:08:42,970
What do you mean?

131
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:47,150
He was born without threads,
a natural outcast.

132
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:48,470
However,

133
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:50,250
except for the one tied to you.

134
00:09:23,750 --> 00:09:25,080
[Chaonan] [Do you want steak?]

135
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,430
[Chaonan] [Or an all-you-can-eat buffet?]

136
00:09:26,430 --> 00:09:27,280
[Chaonan] [Every day?]

137
00:09:27,370 --> 00:09:29,550
Why is he acting crazy
even with a hangover now?

138
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:28,170
[My treat.]

139
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:31,360
[Are you full?]

140
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:34,500
We just came over to see

141
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,540
if there's any room for discussion.

142
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:43,120
If you're going to do things this way,

143
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,290
then we have nothing to talk about.

144
00:09:44,290 --> 00:09:45,320
Please go back.

145
00:09:45,350 --> 00:09:46,140
Please leave.

146
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:48,850
Miss Hong, we came here
today with sincerity,

147
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:51,440
to see how we can cooperate
with you in the future.

148
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,320
Sir,

149
00:09:52,450 --> 00:09:53,540
if you had been sincere,

150
00:09:53,540 --> 00:09:56,040
you wouldn't have used
this kind of ambush tactic today.

151
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:58,620
Please come back next time.
The door is over there.

152
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:00,240
-Please move over there.
-Miss Hong, let's talk again.

153
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,650
Or you can state your conditions.

154
00:10:01,650 --> 00:10:03,320
What are you doing?
Don't be so fierce, okay?

155
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:04,370
What are you doing?

156
00:10:04,370 --> 00:10:05,370
Calm down.

157
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:06,500
Don't push her.

158
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:07,660
Who are you?

159
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,690
Why are you being so fierce to him?

160
00:10:09,690 --> 00:10:10,910
What happened?

161
00:10:11,040 --> 00:10:12,620
-The Chief of Village brought...
-Chief of Village, we...

162
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:14,460
Him here without prior notice,

163
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:16,880
saying they want to talk about
some acquisition agreement.

164
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:20,010
No, I'm such a good old friend
of your grandpa and dad.

165
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:21,630
What's there to be uncomfortable about?

166
00:10:21,630 --> 00:10:24,790
Besides, I'm kindly helping
you coordinate.

167
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,570
Look for yourself.

168
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,210
All the residents

169
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,680
have agreed to the acquisition.

170
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:32,880
-It won't do for only you to stay stuck.
-Chief of Village,

171
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:34,350
we've all heard

172
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:35,120
that you privately

173
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:37,070
went to the 2 neighbors
who didn't want to sell their houses

174
00:10:37,070 --> 00:10:37,920
and told them

175
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:40,010
that if they persuaded us
to sell our house,

176
00:10:40,010 --> 00:10:42,690
Longxing Group would privately
give them a commission.

177
00:10:42,690 --> 00:10:44,960
That's why they agreed to sell.

178
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:47,070
How much money did you take from them

179
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:49,250
to help outsiders force us like this?

180
00:10:49,270 --> 00:10:50,550
What do you mean by that?

181
00:10:50,550 --> 00:10:51,740
What do you mean I took money from them?

182
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:52,570
Didn't you?

183
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:53,610
You'd better make yourself clear!

184
00:10:53,610 --> 00:10:54,680
I'm telling the truth!

185
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,150
I've been the Chief of Village
for over 10 years,

186
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:56,980
fair and square!

187
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:58,240
Don't smear me!

188
00:10:58,260 --> 00:10:59,260
I'm telling you!

189
00:11:00,350 --> 00:11:01,570
What are you talking about?

190
00:11:01,570 --> 00:11:03,130
That's a personal attack!

191
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:04,500
Calm down, guys.

192
00:11:09,310 --> 00:11:11,810
You're really miserable this time.

193
00:11:11,830 --> 00:11:15,490
You seem to easily get involved
in other people's disputes.

194
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:22,560
Thank you, Chief.

195
00:11:26,370 --> 00:11:28,200
Actually, for this whole thing,

196
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:30,670
Zhiling has already gone to
the government agencies, Longxing Group,

197
00:11:30,670 --> 00:11:33,460
and the resident representatives
to get things clear.

198
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:35,960
The whole plan started 3 years ago,

199
00:11:35,990 --> 00:11:37,930
and the acquisition
didn't start until last year.

200
00:11:37,930 --> 00:11:41,660
Actually, most residents
are very willing to cooperate.

201
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,180
Just...

202
00:11:42,210 --> 00:11:43,470
Everyone should talk nicely.

203
00:11:43,470 --> 00:11:45,090
Except for that Miss Hong.

204
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:46,890
No amount of communication works.

205
00:11:46,890 --> 00:11:47,890
Calm down.

206
00:11:48,130 --> 00:11:49,150
I know.

207
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:51,810
You sympathize with Miss Hong
very much, right?

208
00:11:51,810 --> 00:11:54,310
You hope she can keep this old house.

209
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:56,290
But you have to consider others,

210
00:11:56,290 --> 00:11:57,790
who hope to get their houses rebuilt

211
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:59,590
and live in a good house quickly.

212
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:02,990
Everyone has their own stance.
No one is right or wrong.

213
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:05,810
So I advise you,

214
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,130
don't interfere.

215
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,300
Listen to me.

216
00:12:39,070 --> 00:12:41,200
I heard about Keke at the station.

217
00:12:42,750 --> 00:12:45,460
I told you not to interfere
in other people's business.

218
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:46,920
Why won't you just listen?

219
00:13:03,570 --> 00:13:05,060
Or is it that

220
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:08,850
you didn't actually want
to take things as they were,

221
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:11,320
and you just wanted to be a hero,

222
00:13:11,870 --> 00:13:13,820
acting as if you could save them?

223
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:16,670
I didn't want to play the hero.

224
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:18,890
Like I said before,

225
00:13:19,310 --> 00:13:21,300
when I see other people's problems,

226
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,200
I can't just ignore them.

227
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:25,370
Nothing will happen if you don't help.

228
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:26,610
Or is it that

229
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:28,390
if you don't do this...

230
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:32,960
you won't feel your own worth?

231
00:13:46,110 --> 00:13:49,440
You had group activities in class
when you were a kid, right?

232
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:52,580
Do you know the feeling

233
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,300
when you turn around,

234
00:13:54,570 --> 00:13:56,170
seeing everyone has a group,

235
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:59,090
but you're the only one left out?

236
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:03,680
Once or twice is fine.

237
00:14:04,730 --> 00:14:07,370
But this has been my life
since I was little.

238
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:13,000
Everyone has their own partners.

239
00:14:14,190 --> 00:14:15,190
It's just me,

240
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:18,950
not knowing when someone
will come and catch me.

241
00:14:26,830 --> 00:14:28,830
It's like the whole world

242
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:31,010
has nothing to do with me.

243
00:14:34,830 --> 00:14:37,010
That's why I want
to work hard to prove

244
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:39,620
that I still deserve
to live in this world.

245
00:15:07,210 --> 00:15:08,080
Ms. Peggy.

246
00:15:09,020 --> 00:15:12,310
Why did you study psychology
instead of music?

247
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:14,560
I just happened to be assigned to it.

248
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:15,920
Just because of that?

249
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:19,080
Yeah, if I like the major, stick with it.
If I don't, just switch.

250
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,370
What about you?

251
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,250
It's because

252
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:24,280
I want to know others better

253
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:25,880
and know myself better.

254
00:15:27,770 --> 00:15:28,800
Are you serious?

255
00:15:29,790 --> 00:15:30,950
I'm serious.

256
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:31,820
Wait,

257
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:33,020
you can go to any bar

258
00:15:33,050 --> 00:15:34,730
or nightclub to work.

259
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,450
There are plenty of heartbroken,
unemployed, or crazy people

260
00:15:36,450 --> 00:15:37,580
there for you to study,

261
00:15:37,580 --> 00:15:39,110
and you can also make money.

262
00:15:41,750 --> 00:15:43,680
What about knowing myself better?

263
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:50,440
Isn't human interaction like a mirror?

264
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:52,320
When you see other people's problems,

265
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:54,050
can't you reflect on yourself?

266
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:55,850
Do you see now

267
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:56,690
that because of you,

268
00:15:56,690 --> 00:15:59,390
I have been distracted?

269
00:16:00,590 --> 00:16:01,380
Sorry.

270
00:16:13,090 --> 00:16:13,940
Hello?

271
00:16:17,150 --> 00:16:18,680
You prepared so much.

272
00:16:18,710 --> 00:16:19,740
I invited you here specifically

273
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:22,740
